}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}\\,.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (1,4) & =(\\frac{-5+a}{2},\\frac{3+b}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}1=\\frac{-5+a}{2} \\\\ 4=\\frac{3+b}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}a=7 \\\\ b=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $(a,b)=(7,5)$ and $a+b=12.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186515499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1069 "q-216948" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/75/75ea79c4a66a187d5973375c40f49d373cee14f9d15848841616e93a420c6cbd.png)\n\nGiven that $(-3,3)$ is the midpoint of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, find the values of $a$ and $b.$\n\n$a=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,b=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c5f766d1-90d4-56be-969c-e0d6ece7eafd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515597 #edb/ref 1074 "The given points are ${{(a,b)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1},\\,{y}_{1})}$, ${{(0,1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2},\\,{y}_{2})}$ and ${{(-3,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{m},\\,{y}_{m})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\ (-3,3) & =(\\frac{a+0}{2},\\frac{b+1}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding $x$- and $y$-coordinates in the equation above gives us\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-3=\\frac{a}{2} \\\\ 3=\\frac{b+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}a=-6 \\\\ b=5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $a=-6$ and $b=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218651565